{{Documentation/Header}}
A memorial notice box placed at the top of the page of a singer who has passed away. It renders a pale blue {{T|Notify}} box with a candle icon, asks readers to be respectful, and links to the wiki's [[Project:Policy|policies and guidelines]] and the [[Forum:Departure|Departure forum]].

Pages using it are filed under [[:Category:Deceased Utaite]]. Categorization is limited to the main namespace, so the template is safe to demonstrate in documentation.

Unlike the inline badges {{T|Active}}, {{T|Inactive}}, {{T|Hiatus}} and {{T|Graduated}}, this is a full-width notice box and is not part of {{T|Status Templates}}.

==Syntax==
{{T|Deceased|block=1
|v1=種類 =
|v2=ref =
}}

Note that the first parameter name is the Japanese word <code>種類</code> ("type"), not a romanized name.

==Examples==
===Default===
Without parameters the notice reads "utaite", which suits most pages.
{{T|Deceased|_Y_=1}}

===Other singing communities===
<code>種類</code> sets which singing community the person belonged to, so the wording fits the subject — for example <code>youtaite</code> for English-speaking singers or <code>geji</code> for Chinese singers.
{{T|Deceased|_Y_=1|p1=種類 = geji}}
{{T|Deceased|_Y_=1|p1=種類 = youtaite}}

===With a source===
<code>ref</code> appends a citation directly after "as confirmed by reported sources".
<pre>
{{Deceased|ref = <ref>[https://twitter.com/example official announcement]</ref>}}
</pre>
{{Deceased|ref = <ref>[https://twitter.com/example official announcement]</ref>}}



